      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T03:54:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Will,\n\nThanks for the clarification.\n\nI checked the missing `.fop_flags \u003d FOP_DONTCACHE` context. It comes from the following separate patch:\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4166135\n\nAs far as I understand, that patch enables IOCB_DONTCACHE support, while this patch only forwards `vfs_fadvise()` to the backing file in FUSE passthrough mode. These two changes appear to support different functionality, and this patch should not require IOCB_DONTCACHE as a functional dependency.\n\nI also found that the same cherry-pick has already been merged into the `android16-6.12-2025-12` branch:\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4399647\n\nBased on this, could we also merge this patch into the current target branch without adding the IOCB_DONTCACHE dependency?\n\nPlease let me know if there is another required dependency that I missed.\n\nThanks.",
